if I hadn't arrived at 4:30AM on a Friday night, and if the promoter hadn't been working at said time of early morning. In any event this review is going to have to be short and sweet as I still got to see all the bands and go about my day so here it is:
1. My first mistake was leaving my camera at home. I could have taken some pictures inside and I was even offered the use of a camera for review but in the end I forgot to pick it up. However, I made it inside to take some pics of DIO, although no pictures were taken in their absence.
3. I was amazed to see the crowd outside, which was actually quite large for a free gig of this calibre. Sadly, I failed to learn the venue code of conduct of how to handle (not) getting in. First there was the long line of people standing outside. I don’t remember having to wait long
